# ── Cloudinary attachments (optional) ──────────────────────────────
# When both are set, issue attachments upload straight from the browser
# to Cloudinary and get a permanent https URL. Unset, files fall back to
# an in-tab object URL that does not survive a reload.
#
# Both values are public by design — an unsigned preset is meant to be
# readable in the bundle, which is why no API secret is needed here. The
# preset IS the security boundary: set its allowed formats and max file
# size in the console, because anyone reading the bundle can post to it.
#
# Setup:
#   1. cloudinary.com → sign up (free plan, no card)
#   2. Settings → Upload → Upload presets → Add preset
#   3. Set "Signing mode" to Unsigned, then restrict formats and max size
#   4. Copy the cloud name from the dashboard and the preset name below
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=

# ── Neon Postgres (optional; the app runs on localStorage until set) ──
# Paste your Neon connection string to move the data layer off the browser.
# Server-only: do NOT give this a VITE_ prefix. Vite inlines every VITE_*
# variable into the client bundle, where a connection string would be public.
#
# Setup:
#   1. neon.tech → create a project, copy the pooled connection string
#   2. Paste it below
#   3. npm run db:migrate    apply the schema in drizzle/
#   4. npm run db:seed       load the demo dataset (destructive: replaces all)
#
# With this unset every one of those steps is skippable and nothing changes.
# DATABASE_URL=

# ── Landing-page "Request access" form ─────────────────────────────
# Where the form POSTs. The browser calls this directly, so it is public
# by nature and carries the VITE_ prefix — keep it to endpoints that are
# safe to expose. Unset, the form reports a send failure.
VITE_REQUEST_ACCESS_ENDPOINT=
